### Running and inspecting the app by hand.
#
# There is no JSON API (spec §3): the app is used through its screens, in a browser.
# Recipes are in the repo-root justfile (`just` lists them); run them from the repo root.
#
# ── Setup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. First time only: `just setup` (dotnet-ef, the generator's venv, the HTTPS dev cert).
#   2. Start the app over HTTPS, starting the database first: `just run`
#      (the auth cookie is Secure, so plain HTTP won't sign in).
#   3. Sign in at https://localhost:7194/sign-in. Sign-in codes are not emailed in
#      Development: they are in the app's log ("Sign-in email for ...: code 123456").
#   Screens: / (home: invites and groups), /groups/{groupId}, /groups/{groupId}/balances.
#   Creating groups, adding members, inviting and recording expenses have no screen
#   yet (spec §14); data already in the development database stays usable.
#
#   Dev certificate expires 2026-11-13. If HTTPS fails: `just renew-cert`
#
# ── Inspecting the data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   `just events`   the event stream, oldest first
#   `just psql`     a psql shell on the development database
#   `just logs`     the database container's logs
#
#   Inside psql (\x auto gives one-field-per-line output for wide rows, \q quits):
#        \dn                      -- schemas: ledger (Marten), identity (EF), wolverine
#        \dt ledger.*             -- event store and document tables
#
#        -- one row per stream (per group)
#        select id, version, created from ledger.mt_streams;
#
#        -- events for one group, pretty-printed
#        select version, type, jsonb_pretty(data)
#        from ledger.mt_events where stream_id = '<groupId>' order by version;
#
#        -- a group's stored activity (history), pretty-printed
#        select jsonb_pretty(data) from ledger.mt_doc_group_activity where id = '<groupId>';
#
#        -- users, and their pending sign-in codes
#        select "Id", "Email" from identity."AspNetUsers";
#        select * from identity."SignInCodes";
#
# ── Resetting ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   `just rebuild-projections`   rebuild the stored projections from the events
#   `just reset-ledger`          drop all domain data (asks first)

@host = https://localhost:7194

### Health: the app is up and reaches both databases. Expect 200.
GET {{host}}/health
